== limits_of_an_axis_of_dates
error[Z0401]: the `x` axis holds the dates of `day`: the limits, the breaks and the labels of an axis of dates are set with `scale_x(date)`, which is not built yet
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:26
  |
4 | r.plot(x: day, y: level).scale_x(limits: [0, 1])
  |                          ^^^^^^^ not in this build
  |
  = help: an axis of dates chooses its limits and its breaks from the dates drawn; `where` keeps the rows of a range of dates

== the_kind_date
error[Z0401]: `scale_x(date)` is not built yet: an axis of dates comes with the next step of this release
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:34
  |
4 | r.plot(x: day, y: level).scale_x(date)
  |                                  ^^^^ not in this build
  |
  = help: the kinds of scale built so far are `linear`, `log` and `sqrt`

== an_area_up_to_dates
error[Z0401]: `area` fills from its line down to zero, but the `y` axis of this plot holds the dates of `day`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:26
  |
4 | r.plot(x: level, y: day).area()
  |                          ^^^^ needs numbers along `y`
  |
  = help: `points`, `lines` and `step` are placed on a scale of dates; `area` needs a number along `y`, and may have dates along the other axis

