== edges_that_are_dates
error[Z0401]: `ribbon` draws `low` on a linear scale, so `day` must be a Bool, Int or Float variable, but it is a Date
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:38
  |
4 | r.plot(x: day, y: level).ribbon(low: day, high: day)
  |                                      ^^^ not a numeric variable
  |
  = help: the edges of a band are numbers; `r.describe()` lists the types of the variables

== numbers_on_an_axis_of_dates
note: 1 row with NA in day or level dropped (line 4)
error[Z0401]: the plot places `day` on a scale of dates along `x`, but `level`, which `points` maps to `x`, is an Int, which is placed on a linear scale
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:45
  |
4 | r.plot(x: day, y: level).points().points(x: level)
  |                                             ^^^^^ `level` is of another kind
  |
  = help: the layers of a plot share one axis, so what is mapped to `x` must all be categories (a Str or a Category), all be numbers or all be dates (a Date or a DateTime); `category(v)` makes categories of a number

