== a_frame_that_holds_the_dates_as_numbers
error[Z0401]: `points` places `x` on a scale of dates, so `day` of this frame must be a Date or DateTime variable, but it is an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:39
  |
4 | r.plot(x: day, y: level).points(data: frame(day = [1, 2], level = [1, 2]))
  |                                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ its `day` is not dates
  |
  = help: the plot maps `day` to `x` as dates, so the frame of every layer must hold it as a Date or a DateTime; `date(day)` reads dates from text

== a_line_at_a_number_on_dates
note: 1 row with NA in day or level dropped (line 4)
error[Z0401]: `at:` of `vline` is the number 3, but the `x` axis of this plot holds the dates of `day`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:45
  |
4 | r.plot(x: day, y: level).points().vline(at: 3)
  |                                             ^ a number on an axis of dates
  |
  = help: draw the line at each date of a variable, as in `vline(data: events, at: day)`

