== a_line_at_text
error[Z0401]: `vline` draws a line at each value of `at:` on the `x` axis, so `site` must be a Bool, Int, Float, Date or DateTime variable, but it is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:36
  |
4 | r.plot(x: day, y: level).vline(at: site)
  |                                    ^^^^ not a number or a date
  |
  = help: a reference line stands at a number or at a date; `r.describe()` lists the types of the variables

== a_colour_by_dates
error[Z0401]: `plot` shows `color` as categories or on a continuous scale, so `day` must be a Bool, Int, Float, Str or Category variable, but it is a Date
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:33
  |
4 | r.plot(x: day, y: level, color: day).points()
  |                                 ^^^ no colour scale for this type
  |
  = help: a colour scale of dates is not in this release yet; `r.describe()` lists the types of the variables
